L10: [Submitted on 19 Nov 2025 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 12 Apr 2026 (this version, v2)]
L11: # Title:Fourier-KAN-Mamba: A Novel State-Space Equation Approach for Time-Series Anomaly Detection
L12: 
L13: Authors:cite6†Xiancheng Wang , cite7†Lin Wang , cite8†Rui Wang , cite9†Zhibo Zhang , cite10†Minghang Zhao L14: 
L15: View a PDF of the paper titled Fourier-KAN-Mamba: A Novel State-Space Equation Approach for Time-Series Anomaly Detection, by Xiancheng Wang and 4 other authors
L16: 
L17: cite11†No PDF available, click to view other formats L18: > Abstract:Time-series anomaly detection plays a critical role in numerous real-world applications, including industrial monitoring and fault diagnosis. Recently, Mamba-based state-space models have shown remarkable efficiency in long-sequence modeling. However, directly applying Mamba to anomaly detection tasks still faces challenges in capturing complex temporal patterns and nonlinear dynamics.
L19: In this paper, we propose Fourier-KAN-Mamba, a novel hybrid architecture that integrates Fourier layer, Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks (KAN), and Mamba selective state-space model. The Fourier layer extracts multi-scale frequency features, KAN enhances nonlinear representation capability, and a temporal gating control mechanism further improves the model's ability to distinguish normal and anomalous patterns.
L20: Extensive experiments on MSL, SMAP, and SWaT datasets demonstrate that our method significantly outperforms existing state-of-the-art approaches.
L21: > Keywords: time-series anomaly detection, state-space model, Mamba, Fourier transform, Kolmogorov-Arnold Network
L22: Comments:  | We request withdrawal because we identified a flaw in the theoretical analysis of the anomaly-score identification mechanism. This part was supported mainly by metric observations without sufficient visual or empirical verification, which may affect the reliability of the related conclusions
